menu "eink-weather bring-up"

    config APP_DIAG_ONLY
        bool "Run the panel wiring diagnostics instead of displaying; never refreshes the panel"
        default n
        help
            Electrical diagnostic mode. app_main() prints the boot banner, runs
            epd_dc_diag(), epd_rst_diag() and epd_dcscan() over bit-banged GPIO
            and stops: no epd_init(), no epd_display(), no refresh, ever. The
            panel is left powered off (POF) and in its post-reset idle state,
            so the mode is safe to repeat as often as needed -- unlike a
            refresh, which ages the glass and must stay rare.

            The question it answers: does the controller see the D/C line at
            all? Single-byte commands (PON, DRF, POF) demonstrably work on this
            board while every data byte -- init parameters and image bytes
            alike -- appears to be ignored, which is exactly what a D/C line
            stuck low at the controller would look like: every byte is then
            read as a command.

            epd_dc_diag() answers it without refreshing by using the BUSY
            power-on signature as an oracle: it sends 0x04 (PON) sometimes as a
            command and sometimes as a data byte and watches whether the
            controller powers up. See components/epd_uc8179/epd_diag.c.

            The other two narrow down the answer. epd_rst_diag() asks whether
            the hardware reset pulse reaches the controller at all -- RST and
            D/C are adjacent contacts on the panel FPC, so two dead lines mean
            a mechanical fault where one dead line does not -- by timing the
            BUSY_N low pulse that POF produces with and without a reset in
            between. epd_dcscan() drives each free GPIO as a second D/C line
            in turn, to exclude a board revision that wires D/C elsewhere.

endmenu
